<title>SINGAPORE: EU's Brittan says 'very good progress' on infotech.</title>
<headline>EU's Brittan says 'very good progress' on infotech.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade negotiators are making &quot;very good&quot; progress towards an agreement to liberalise world trade in information technology, European Commissioner Sir Leon Brittan told reporters on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Asked how talks on information technology were progressing, Brittan replied: &quot;Very good.&quot;</p>
<p>Pressed to say whether a deal had been clinched, he added: &quot;Not yet. But we're making very good progress.&quot;</p>
<p>Brittan was speaking to reporters as he arrived for talks during the inaugural ministerial meeting of ther World Trade Organisation with acting U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky and Canadian and Japanese ministers.</p>
<p>Barshefsky also characterised progress on the information technology talks as good.</p>
</text>
